section.subsection:
For purposes of this section:

"Natural disaster" means:
an explosion;
fire;
a flood;
a storm;
a tornado;
winds;
an earthquake;
lightning;
any adverse weather event; or
any event similar to an event described in this Subsection (1), as determined by the commission by rule made in accordance with Title 63G, Chapter 3, Utah Administrative Rulemaking Act.
"Natural disaster damage" means any physical harm to property caused by a natural disaster.
